    "reviewed_deltas": [
      {
        "area": "Own tiers, parent/child and one effective layer",
        "result": "PASS",
        "finding": "The three marks share one actual trait variant and the same I–IV parent melee_power_level_modifier values .12/.16/.20/.24, formatted +12/+16/+20/+24%. The wrapper replaces the parent proc predicate with the weapon-special melee check while preserving the held-slot gates. Its child uses stack_offset=-1 and max_stacks=1; the initial child is a zero-effect placeholder. The matching parent tier is supplied to the child and replaces the child conditional .20 fallback because neither template has a static stat_buffs contribution. There is one effective tier term, not a parent constant plus child fallback."
      },
      {
        "area": "Three actual special attacks and attack-type coverage",
        "result": "PASS",
        "finding": "The actual UI bindings are Delver’s Pickaxe Branx Mk Ia, Borovian Mk III, and Karsolas Mk II. Their weapon-special sweeps use the uppercut profile on Branx and hook-pull profiles on the other two; each profile sets weapon_special=true and dispatches melee attacks through ActionSweep. Ordinary light/heavy or charged attacks and push-followups do not proc or refresh, though melee attacks may use the active modifier while the pickaxe is held. Pure push is attack_type=push and does not proc or consume this melee power key."
      },
      {
        "area": "First hit, refresh, strict expiry and switching",
        "result": "PASS",
        "finding": "Attack damage and HitReaction resolve before on_hit, so the triggering hit is not retroactively boosted. An accepted special hit activates or refreshes the one child at event-handling time; re-hits refresh the same 3.5-second timer even at the one-effective-layer cap. Expiry uses remove_t<t: equality is not yet expired, and later stat reads follow cache updates. Switching away disables the held-gated proc/stat while the timer continues; switching back before expiry may restore the remaining effect after the cache update. Destroying the parent removes its externally controlled child."
      },
      {
        "area": "Power math and saved cleave budget",
        "result": "PASS",
        "finding": "The native power-type curve produces S before additive melee-power modifiers, so S_after=S×(1+q+p). At tier IV with S=100 and no other same-key term, the input becomes 124; with q=.20, 120 becomes 144, which is +20% relative to 120 rather than a further ×1.24. The source routes power into damage, impact, and cleave consumers without implying equal final health damage, stagger, or target counts. ActionSweep samples its cleave budget at swing start; a later proc does not automatically recalculate that saved budget, while later damage/impact reads may see an updated cache and server correction has its separately documented recomputation path."
      },
      {
        "area": "RAW reconstruction and comparison",
        "result": "PASS",
        "finding": "The paired name/description keys and hashes match the fixed 1.13.1 English and zh-TW RAW. The four tier placeholders reconstruct to +12%, +16%, +20%, +24%, with a 3.5-second duration. The comparison distinguishes RAW-stated trigger/value/time from first-hit, cache, switch, strict-expiry, and cleave timing that the text does not cover; it does not present those omissions as RAW errors or add an empty errata section."
      },
      {
        "area": "Formal pages, map, reverse index and icon identity",
        "result": "PASS",
        "finding": "All seven formal pages match the approved config for the actual three marks, tier values, special-action differences, player trigger/lifecycle text, math, and source conclusions. The shared map has exactly one melee blessing entry, one trait variant, and three bindings for marks m1/m2/m3. The three rows and reverse Delver’s Pickaxe page link to the Torment overview/variant correctly; the shared blessing indexes and translation index contain the expected rows and RAW key. Icon content identity weapon_trait_214 is kept as its source path, separate from the verified attachment URL."
      }
